<title>PERU: Peru's August coffee output rises 24.4 percent.</title>
<headline>Peru's August coffee output rises 24.4 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's August coffee production rose 24.4 percent to 3,634 tonnes from the same month last year, Agriculture Ministry said Wednesday.</p>
<p>Coffee output for the first eight months was up 10.9 percent at 105,663 tonnes compared to the same period of 1995.</p>
<p>Coffee exports rose 14.5 percent in August to 16,923 tonnes, worth $37.2 million, while exports in the first seven months gained 35.6 percent to 71,147 tonnes, worth $157.5 million, the ministry said.</p>
<p>Peru, whose principal coffee harvest is between April and November, is South America's number four producer after Brazil, Colombia and Ecuador, according to the government.</p>
<p>--Andrew Cawthorne, Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134</p>
